<title>UK: UK's LASMO reports successful Algeria drill.</title>
<headline>UK's LASMO reports successful Algeria drill.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Oil exploration company LASMO Plc said on Tuesday it had reported successful drilling results in a well in the Ghadames Basin in Algeria.</p>
<p>LASMO said the well, HBNSE-1  in block 404, was drilled to a total depth of 3,310 metres and was tested at a rate of 17,092 barrels of 47.6 degree API oil per day and 37.5 million cubic feet of gas per day.</p>
<p>LASMO holds 25 percent stake in the discovery.</p>
<p>The company's share price opened strong and reached a high of 277 pence, 6 1/2 higher than its Monday's closing of 270p.</p>
<p>---London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
